$$SYNTAX-LEVEL 2
*(mgdb-archive
<main class="mgdb-page mgdb-hub-page mgdb-archive-page" id="archive-main">
  <nav class="mgdb-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/data_center/">Data hubs</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><span aria-current="page">Archived data hubs</span>
  </nav>

  <section class="mgdb-hero" aria-labelledby="archive-title">
    <div class="mgdb-hero-emblem">
      <svg class="archive-hero-mark" viewBox="0 0 132 116" role="img" aria-label="Five archival collection drawers">
        <rect x="14" y="10" width="104" height="96" rx="10" fill="#f4edd0" stroke="#a96919" stroke-width="4" />
        <g>
          <rect x="24" y="20" width="84" height="14" rx="4" fill="#501719" /><rect x="24" y="38" width="84" height="14" rx="4" fill="#2f5e2a" /><rect x="24" y="56" width="84" height="14" rx="4" fill="#a96919" /><rect x="24" y="74" width="84" height="14" rx="4" fill="#501719" /><rect x="24" y="92" width="84" height="6" rx="3" fill="#2f5e2a" />
        </g>
        <g fill="#f4edd0"><rect x="59" y="24" width="14" height="5" rx="2" /><rect x="59" y="42" width="14" height="5" rx="2" /><rect x="59" y="60" width="14" height="5" rx="2" /><rect x="59" y="78" width="14" height="5" rx="2" /></g>
      </svg>
      <strong>Archived<br />Data Hubs</strong>
    </div>
    <div class="mgdb-hero-body">
      <h1 id="archive-title">Archived data hubs</h1>
      <p class="mgdb-hero-description">MaizeGDB does not delete scientific data. These five collections preserve records, evidence, and interfaces that remain important for reproducing earlier research, even though they are no longer actively updated. Each one links to the current resource that replaced it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="mgdb-section-tabs" aria-label="Sections on this page">
    <a href="#archive-collections" class="is-current" aria-current="true">Collections</a>
    <a href="#archive-use">Using the archive</a>
    <a href="#archive-metrics">Metrics</a>
    <a href="#archive-related">Related resources</a>
  </nav>

  <section id="archive-collections" aria-labelledby="archive-collections-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="archive-collections-title">Collections</h2></div>
    </div>

    <p class="mgdb-note"><strong>There is no search on this page.</strong> Each archive keeps its own search over its own records; use the collection you need. For a new analysis, start from the current resource named on the card instead.</p>

    <div class="mgdb-card-grid archive-collection-grid">
      <article class="mgdb-card archive-collection-card archive-bac">
        <div class="archive-card-top"><span class="mgdb-pill mgdb-pill-info">Physical mapping</span></div>
        <h3>BAC clone archive</h3>
        <p>Bacterial artificial chromosome clone names, synonyms, accessions, sequences, and physical-map relationships from historical B73 assemblies.</p>
        <div class="archive-card-actions"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="/data_center/bac">Open BAC archive</a><a href="/genome/assembly/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0">Current B73 reference <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card archive-collection-card archive-cytogenetic">
        <div class="archive-card-top"><span class="mgdb-pill mgdb-pill-ok">Chromosome biology</span></div>
        <h3>Cytogenetics resources</h3>
        <p>Cytological maps, chromosome landmarks, karyotype and FISH imagery, structural-variant stocks, and foundational cytogenetics references.</p>
        <div class="archive-card-actions"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="/data_center/cytogenetic">Open Cytogenetics</a><a href="/genome">Current genome resources <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card archive-collection-card archive-est">
        <div class="archive-card-top"><span class="mgdb-pill mgdb-pill-warn">Transcript evidence</span></div>
        <h3>Expressed sequence tags</h3>
        <p>EST names, sequence identifiers, GenBank accessions, legacy library patterns, annotations, detected loci, and mapped transcript evidence.</p>
        <div class="archive-card-actions"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="/data_center/est">Open EST collection</a><a href="/expression">Current expression data <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card archive-collection-card archive-overgo">
        <div class="archive-card-top"><span class="mgdb-pill">Mapping probes</span></div>
        <h3>Overgo probe archive</h3>
        <p>Overgo probe names and short sequences used to connect clones, loci, physical maps, and early maize genome projects.</p>
        <div class="archive-card-actions"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="/data_center/overgo">Open Overgo archive</a><a href="/data_center/marker">Current marker search <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card archive-collection-card archive-ssr">
        <div class="archive-card-top"><span class="mgdb-pill mgdb-pill-info">Microsatellite markers</span></div>
        <h3>SSR marker archive</h3>
        <p>Simple sequence repeat names, synonyms, motifs, primers, gel patterns, mapped-marker files, and historical mapping protocols.</p>
        <div class="archive-card-actions"><a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-primary" href="/data_center/ssr">Open SSR archive</a><a href="/data_center/marker">Current marker search <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="archive-use" class="mgdb-prose-layout" aria-labelledby="archive-use-title">
    <div class="mgdb-prose">
      <h2 id="archive-use-title" class="mgdb-leaf-heading">Using the archive</h2>
      <p>Use these collections when following older publications, clone names, probes, marker systems, cytological maps, or legacy accessions.</p>
      <p>Legacy identifiers and coordinates may refer to older assemblies, map versions, nomenclature, or laboratory methods. Record the collection name, identifiers, map or assembly version, and access date when using archived material.</p>
      <p>Follow linked loci, genes, sequences, references, and maps to understand how a historical record relates to current MaizeGDB data.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="mgdb-aside-card archive-help-card">
      <h3>If an identifier does not resolve</h3>
      <p>Contact MaizeGDB with the identifier, the publication it appeared in, and the collection you were searching.</p>
      <a class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" href="/contact">Contact MaizeGDB</a>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section id="archive-metrics" aria-labelledby="archive-metrics-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="archive-metrics-title">Metrics</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-metric-grid">
      @(metric-card
        <article class="mgdb-metric mgdb-tone-$(tone)">
          <div>
            <strong class="mgdb-metric-value">$(value)</strong>
            <h3>$(label)</h3>
            <p>$(detail)</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      )
    </div>

    <p class="mgdb-small mgdb-muted archive-metric-note">Each figure is the count its own archive reports, taken from that hub&#8217;s query. Cytogenetics has no collection of its own to count &#8212; it draws on stocks, images, and references held elsewhere.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="archive-related" class="mgdb-hub-related" aria-labelledby="archive-related-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="archive-related-title">Related resources</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-resource-panel">
      <div class="mgdb-resource-list">
        <a href="/data_center/">
          <strong>Data hubs</strong>
          <span>Every active MaizeGDB data hub, grouped by the question it answers</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/data_center/marker">
          <strong>Markers and probes</strong>
          <span>The current home for marker records, including those first typed here</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/genome">
          <strong>Genome data hub</strong>
          <span>Assemblies and annotations that replaced the physical maps</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/expression">
          <strong>Expression data hub</strong>
          <span>RNA-seq atlases in place of expressed sequence tag evidence</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/contact">
          <strong>Contact MaizeGDB</strong>
          <span>Reach the curation team about a record you cannot resolve</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
)
